==English==
{{was wotd|2012|December|28}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|brawne|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|braon||slice of meat, fleshy part, buttock|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|frk|en}} *{{term||brādon}}, accusative form of *{{term||brādo|roasted meat, ham}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*brēdô||meat, roast}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*bhre-||to burn, heat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*bureue-||to boil, bubble, burn}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term/t|goh|brāto||tender meat}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Braten||roast|lang=de}}), {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term/t|ang|brǣd||flesh, meat}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|bráð||raw meat|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɔːn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Strong [[muscle]]s or [[lean]] [[flesh]], especially of the arm, leg or thumb.
# Physical [[strength]]; [[muscularity]].
#* '''2000''', Stephanie Laurens, ''A Secret Love'', Avon Books (2000), ISBN 0380805707, [http://books.google.com/books?id=UIA1KBh1iLAC&pg=PA349 page 349]:
#*: The man was a bruiser, the sort who'd learned his science in tavern brawls. Given his size and lack of agility, he relied on his '''brawn''' to win. In any wrestling match, Crowley would triumph easily.
#* '''2008''', Michael Mandaville, ''Stealing Thunder'', Dog Ear Publishing (2008), ISBN 9781598585353, [http://books.google.com/books?id=U-xdpBsgoGUC&pg=PA562 page 562]:
#*: The two men were husky, picked for their '''brawn''' by the little man who sauntered into the room.
#* '''2010''', Martin Pasko & Robert Greenberger, ''The Essential Superman Encyclopedia'', Del Ray (2010), ISBN 9780345501080, [http://books.google.com/books?id=aknpy8JiMWEC&pg=PA218 page 218]:
#*: The youth agreed to the scheme and used his '''brawn''' to begin moving pieces into place, starting by moving the planet Rann into the Thanagarian star system {{...}}
# {{context|chiefly|British|lang=en}} [[head cheese]]; a [[terrine]] made from the [[head]] of a [[pig]] or [[calf]]; originally [[boar]]'s meat.

